# Phase-4 replay archive — crafting: a consumed FLOOR material leaves the
# world through ONE craft report. Before the crafting domain, the game's
# RecipeItem.UseItem called Body.DropItem + Destroy per material and every
# per-call report fired: the "drop" report materialized a ghost of the
# destroyed item on the peers (the material was destroyed, never dropped), and
# the destroy report raced it. The craft report carries the complete terminal
# state (the Destroyed entry), the host removes the world-table entry and the
# WHOLE report relays once (source excluded) — the peers destroy their copies.
#
# Fossil of: CraftSyncSimulationTests.GuestCraft_FloorMaterialDestroyed_WorldTableRemovedAndRelayed
# Mechanism: CraftSyncService.FireCraftReportReceived — WorldDestroy → RemoveWorldItemLocal, then the whole-report relay
#            (Runtime/Session/Items/CraftSyncService.cs)

@0 spawn g1 42 cloth 1.0
@33 craft g1 craft d:42 p:44:bandage:1.0
@66 expect no_host_table 42 within 500
@66 expect received g2 CraftReport 1 within 500
@66 expect_no_reject g1
